            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0515" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.34/422: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cable</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-09T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1927—7
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>11. Department’s telegram No. 9, dated March 1, 3 p.m. Please inform Department
                    of present status of matter. Representative of <pb facs="0516" n="430"
                        xml:id="pg430"/> Bethlehem interests in Washington states that he has good
                    reason for believing that the board which is supposed to receive and report upon
                    all tenders did not even pass upon his company’s bids.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
